 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 666485,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Given the following code, how many times does the print statement execute?\n<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">i = 1\nwhile i &lt;= 5:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;j = 1\n&nbsp;&nbsp;while i + j &lt;= 5:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print(i, j)\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;j += 1\n&nbsp;&nbsp;i += 1\n</pre>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1328508,
     "content_html": "5",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "The outer loop executes 5 times. For each outer loop's iteration, the inner loop, which contains the print statement, executes while <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">i + j</code> is less than or equal to 5. How many times is the <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">print()</code> statement executed?"
    },
    {
     "id": 1328509,
     "content_html": "10",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "The combination of <code>i</code> and <code>j</code> values, <code>(i, j)</code>, that meet the inner and outer loop conditions are as follows: <br> <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), </code> <br>\n<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(2, 1), (2, 2), (2, 3), </code><br>\n<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(3, 1), (3, 2), </code><br>\n<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(4, 1)</code>\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1328510,
     "content_html": "25",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "The outer loop executes 5 times (<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">i = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5</code>) and the inner loop executes while <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">i + j &lt;= 5</code>. As j's value increases, the number of iterations that the inner loop executes decreases. <br>\n<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), </code> <br>\n<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(2, 1), (2, 2), (2, 3), </code><br>\n<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(3, 1), (3, 2), </code><br>\n<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(4, 1)</code>"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The combination of <code>i</code> and <code>j</code> values, <code>(i, j)</code>, that meet the inner and outer loop conditions are as follows: <br> <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), </code> <br>\n<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(2, 1), (2, 2), (2, 3), </code><br>\n<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(3, 1), (3, 2), </code><br>\n<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(4, 1)</code>\n"
    }
